# print_services: one semantic print surface, many realizations [SPEC:CXC-PRINT-SERVICES]

> **[PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED].** This document was written into `corpora/platform-specs/` because that
> is where its neighbours live, not because the placement was ruled — see [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT] for
> the standing note on this directory's unratified filename numbering. Filename `83-print-services.lts`
> was chosen as the first non-colliding slot after `82-document-store-containment.lts`; it is provisional.
>
> **v1 build dispatched 2026-08-22, IN PARALLEL with this spec being made build-ready — this is the
> FROZEN contract the build is dispatched against.** print_services itself (bus contract, HP direct-IPP
> backend, Elegoo status-only backend) and printer discovery are moving to `spec-authored`/build; the
> ImageWriter direct peer, the Cashino CSN-A2, and the classic Mac bus peer remain `proposed` — designed
> but not being built in this pass. Every evidence slot on every node stays named `EMPTY` until a real
> bench fills it: this document being build-ready is not a claim that anything has touched hardware yet.
> That is the whole point of [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE] applied to this slice: *designed*,
> *build-ready*, and *implemented* must never be visually indistinguishable in a spec that reads as finished.

- lifecycle-position: spec-authored
- placement: UNRATIFIED
- the-model: a bus-native print surface. Each physical printer is a co-equal bus PEER (announce-then-bind), presenting `print_services/<printer>/submit` (content-first: accepts text / markdown / html / svg / scene, returns a job_id), `.../status` (ready|busy|paper_out|offline), `.../jobs` (recent history). This is [CXC-HAL-ACTUATE] — a printer is an output actuator peer.
- content-first: submit SEMANTIC content and let the realizer rasterize — NOT file-first. Generalizes [CXC-VISION-SEMANTIC-REALIZATION] to paper: one value flows to screen, needle, numeral, AND print, and the print realizer is just one more backend for the same semantic submission.
- realization-spectrum: ONE surface, three backends. (1) wrap-an-OS-driver — a modern printer reached via CUPS `lp`. (2) speak-native-protocol — a networked printer reached via its own protocol, e.g. SDCP for resin 3D. (3) raw-hardware — a dumb/vintage printer reached via its raw serial command set plus a ComposeUX Canvas backend that rasterizes to the device's dot-graphics. The backend is the realization; the surface is the meaning, and a caller submitting content never needs to know which of the three answered.
- policy-cap-not-gate: print-freely, cap-safely. A per-period page/resource cap is the runaway-loop safety net, NOT an approval queue — nothing here blocks on human sign-off before a job runs. Adopted from Haven's print-service DP-PRINT-2 as prior art for the content-first plus cap-safely plus wrap-vs-native pattern; Haven is a SEPARATE project and print_services depends on none of its code.
- reference-provenance: the Haven project's `haven_print` (CUPS-wrap) and `print_3d_service` (SDCP-native) at ~/haven were studied as prior art for the three-backend split and the cap-safely policy. Nothing in this file imports, depends on, or forks Haven code.
- pre-integration-questions: ANSWERED, not open — this is a design pass. The three realization backends (see realization-spectrum), the cap policy (see policy-cap-not-gate), and the content-first submit contract (see content-first) are the design; no unmade decision is silently carried forward here.
- bus-surface-registry: RETAINED `print_services/registry/<id>` = `{id, kind, width, color, graphics, dpi, content_types[], status_ns, backend, heartbeat_ts}`; heartbeat republish on an age contract (default 30s); tombstone published on graceful exit.
- bus-surface-submit: `print_services/<id>/submit` = `{job_id?, content_type: text|markdown|html|svg|pdf|scene, content, options?{copies?}}`. `content_type` is the PLATFORM union; each backend advertises the SUBSET it accepts via its registry descriptor (see [CXC-PRINT-DISCOVERY] descriptor-carries-capabilities) — HP: text/markdown/html/svg/pdf; the raw-hardware peers (ImageWriter/CSN-A2): scene/text via their Canvas backends.
- bus-surface-result: `print_services/<id>/result` = `{job_id, status: submitted|done|error, detail?, pages?}`; in-memory job history, last 50 retained.
- bus-surface-status: RETAINED `print_services/<id>/status` = `{state: ready|busy|paper_out|offline, ts}`.
- policy-cap: per-period page cap, env `PRINT_SERVICES_DAILY_CAP` default 100, enforced at submit; error-not-gate — the cap is the safety net named in policy-cap-not-gate, never an approval queue.
- service-shape: bare-Python service at `services/print_services/`; MQTT client via env `COMPOSEIO_MQTT_URL`; `/api/v1/status` HTTP endpoint (hostname plus git-sha, the P-c identity shape) on env `PRINT_SERVICES_PORT` default 8425.
- v1-scope: HP backend FULL — driverless IPP-Everywhere direct to (a private LAN address, not published), NO CUPS. Elegoo backend STATUS-ONLY — SDCP status to (a private LAN address, not published); 3D print-submission is deferred to v2 (needs slicing/upload).
- reachability-evidence: MEASURED 2026-08-22 from (a private host name, not published) — see [DEC-(a private host name, not published)-STAYS-ON-LOCAL-SUBNET]; HP (a private LAN address, not published) reachable via IPP/IPPS/raw, Elegoo (a private LAN address, not published) reachable via SDCP. This is the pre-integration reachability confirmation for v1-scope.
- evidence-ipp-hp: EMPTY
- evidence-native-3d: EMPTY
- evidence-raw-imagewriter: EMPTY
- evidence-cap-enforced: EMPTY
- see-also: [CXC-HAL-ACTUATE], [CXC-VISION-SEMANTIC-REALIZATION]

