## [CXC-PRINT-DISCOVERY] Discovering printers on the bus — announce-then-bind, not a registry

- part-of: [CXC-PRINT-SERVICES]
- lifecycle-position: spec-authored
- build-status: built in print_services v1
- the-model: discovery IS announce-then-bind ([CXC-VISION-ANNOUNCE-BIND]), NOT a central registry service — a registry would be a center, and there is none. Each printer peer publishes a RETAINED descriptor to `print_services/registry/<printer>` on join. A participant subscribes `print_services/registry/+` and receives the full roster immediately (retained means new subscribers catch up), plus live join/leave.
- descriptor-carries-capabilities: id, kind (thermal|impact|laser|resin|fdm), width (58mm|80mm|letter|A4|page), color (mono|color), graphics (bool), dpi, content-types (text|markdown|html|svg|pdf|scene — the PLATFORM union; a given descriptor advertises the SUBSET that backend accepts, e.g. HP: text/markdown/html/svg/pdf, ImageWriter/CSN-A2: scene/text), status-namespace, realization-backend. Capabilities let a publisher pick the right printer for a job.
- availability-is-state: a printer's presence is STATE on the bus, never a poll — retained descriptor plus an age contract ([DEC-IMPLEMENT-MQTT-RETAIN-WITH-AN-AGE-CONTRACT]): periodic heartbeat re-publish; a silent printer ages out; graceful exit publishes a tombstone clearing the retained descriptor. This is freshness-verdict-is-state ([DEC-A-FRESHNESS-VERDICT-IS-STATE-NOT-A-HANDLER]).
- no-center: the roster is EMERGENT from peer announcements on the shared namespace; a "directory" view may aggregate for convenience but holds no authority.
- optional-capability-routing: submit MAY target a specific printer (`print_services/<printer>/submit`) OR a capability selector (e.g. `to: any-thermal`) resolved against the descriptors — a policy layer, not core.
- pre-integration-questions: ANSWERED — the announce-then-bind mechanism (see the-model), the descriptor shape (see descriptor-carries-capabilities), and the age-contract freshness model (see availability-is-state) are the design. No open pre-wiring decision remains.
- evidence-retained-roster: EMPTY
- evidence-ageout: EMPTY
- evidence-capability-routing: EMPTY
- see-also: [CXC-VISION-ANNOUNCE-BIND], [DEC-IMPLEMENT-MQTT-RETAIN-WITH-AN-AGE-CONTRACT], [CXC-PRINT-SERVICES]

