## [DEC-PRINT-SERVICES-HOOKUP-MODEL] Decision — print_services peers connect directly, never via another device

- lifecycle-position: decided
- decision: print_services is a bus-native surface where each printer is a DIRECT co-equal peer that owns itself; the ImageWriter connects directly (Mac out of the print path), NOT via the Mac. Content-first submit; three realization backends (CUPS-wrap / native-protocol / raw-serial-plus-Canvas-backend); print-freely-cap-safely policy.
- rationale: a printer is a fleet resource and must not depend on another device's uptime — routing through the Mac would gate "can the fleet print?" on "is the Mac on?", the exact accidental coupling decentralization dissolves. The bus decouples what 1984 coupled.
- alternative-rejected: ImageWriter-via-the-Mac — reintroduces a Mac-uptime dependency; kept only as a rasterization REFERENCE (see [CXC-PRINT-IMAGEWRITER] rasterization-reference) and a possible bootstrap, not the target.
- human: David chose print_services (plural) and the direct-module model over the via-Mac alternative, 2026-08-22.
- ratified: David 2026-08-22 — kicked off the build+deploy.
- driverless-hp-refinement: the HP is IPP-Everywhere, so the HP backend uses direct IPP with NO CUPS and NO Haven dependency (refines gate-2 reuse boundary).
- relates-to: [DEC-(a private host name, not published)-STAYS-ON-LOCAL-SUBNET]
- see-also: [CXC-PRINT-SERVICES], [CXC-PRINT-IMAGEWRITER], [DX-LEAF-OWNS-BEHAVIOR]

